.TH LIBMPQ__ARCHIVE_COMPRESSION_ALLOWED 3 2026-09-09 "The MoPaQ archive library"
.SH NAME
libmpq__archive_compression_allowed \- query whether writer compression is allowed
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B
#include <libmpq/mpq.h>
.sp
.BI "int32_t libmpq__archive_compression_allowed("
.BI "        uint32_t                    " "archive_version",
.BI "        uint32_t                    " "compression_mask",
.BI "        libmpq_compression_policy_t " "policy"
.BI ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The policy type libmpq_compression_policy_t is a signed int32_t.
.PP
The version uses LIBMPQ_ARCHIVE_VERSION_ONE (0) or
LIBMPQ_ARCHIVE_VERSION_TWO (1), not the one-based archive-version accessor.
A zero mask selects raw storage. LZMA uses LIBMPQ_COMPRESSION_LZMA (0x100),
an exclusive selector available only for v2; it serializes as method 0x12.
.PP
LIBMPQ_COMPRESSION_POLICY_STANDARD (0) is the default writer policy.
For MPQ v2+ it permits zlib, PKWARE, bzip2, LZMA, and Huffman paired with
mono or stereo ADPCM. Its fixed SPARSE forms are SPARSE alone (0x20),
SPARSE with zlib (0x22), and SPARSE with bzip2 (0x30).
.PP
LIBMPQ_COMPRESSION_POLICY_EXTENDED (1) permits additional implemented
combinations, including standalone Huffman in v2. These may be less
interoperable with StormLib or other MPQ implementations; they are not
classified as invalid MPQ.
.PP
Both policies retain normal v1 compression-mask semantics, allowing other
valid combinations such as SPARSE with Huffman (0x21) or PKWARE (0x28).
In MPQ v2+, EXTENDED permits the broader valid lossless SPARSE combinations.
Unknown bits, conflicting ADPCM channels, SPARSE combined with either
ADPCM bit, and v2 masks containing both zlib and bzip2 are rejected.
SPARSE precedes other stages, so lossy
ADPCM cannot safely preserve its control bytes. The zlib/bzip2 combination
could otherwise emit method 0x12, reserved for LZMA. Invalid policies or
unsupported archive versions are rejected too.
.PP
Select EXTENDED for a writer by setting
LIBMPQ_ARCHIVE_CREATE_COMPRESSION_EXTENDED in its archive-creation flags.
The options struct layout is unchanged. Both sector selections are validated.
Input-specific WAVE and file-storage constraints still apply.
.PP
If skipped stages leave a method disallowed by the policy, the writer stores
the original sector raw. The first WAVE sector stays lossless, using zlib
instead of standalone Huffman under STANDARD v2.
Readers remain permissive and never require this policy setting.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns 1 if the compression selection is allowed for the archive version
and policy, otherwise 0.
